8
00:46:17,142 --> 00:46:23,142
Self, played by Arnaud Desplechin.

9
00:52:04,285 --> 00:52:10,285
Self, played by David Fincher.

10
00:57:51,428 --> 00:57:57,428
Hitchcock/Truffaut is a 1966 book by François Truffaut about Alfred Hitchcock,
originally released in French as Le Cinéma selon Alfred Hitchcock.

11
01:03:38,571 --> 01:03:44,571
First published by Éditions Robert Laffont, it is based on a 1962 dialogue between Hitchcock and Truffaut,
in which the two directors spent a week in a room at Universal Studios talking about movies.

12
01:09:25,714 --> 01:09:31,714
The book walks through all of Hitchcock's films, from
his early British period to Torn Curtain.

13
01:15:12,857 --> 01:15:18,857
After Hitchcock's death, Truffaut updated the book with a new preface and final chapter on Hitchcock's
later films Topaz, Frenzy and Family Plot, as well as his unrealized project The Short Night.
